{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035809-art-and-the-umbra","id":1035809,"title":"Art and The Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-21T13:20:35-08:00","id":1035809,"title":"Art and The Umbra","content":"When I say &quot;Art&quot;, in this context I mean the product of an Artist's endeavors, not the ars magicka. Although, since this is Mage, they could be used as one and the same. Further, I could argue that they are one and the same.<br /> <br /> Consider that one interpretation of the Umbra is that of the spiritual reflection of human (and possibly non-human) belief. The Underworld exists because people think there's a place people go to after death, Maya is forged from their dreams, there are a host of heavens and hells represented in the High Umbra (and elsewhere) that reflect different mythologies and religions, etc. The more people believe in something, the greater it's fueled by imagination, and the greater its presence in the spirit world. This isn't necessarily true - or, if it is true, only one side of a richer and more complicated Truth - but it can and has been argued. This is not new.<br /> <br /> But it got me thinking about Art specifically - the product of artistic endeavor, whether that be painted, audible, textual, interactive, or some combination of the same. Given that Art pieces grasp our imaginations so, would that mean that pieces of Art have spiritual reflections in the Umbra?<br /> <br /> Could a Mage use Spirit 3 to step into a Rembrandt, and find herself in the Umbral reflection of that scene? Would she be able to talk to the figures depicted within it? Bathe in a painted stream? Eat the fruit from a still life bowl? Could a Virtual Adept download himself, Tron-style, into the game map of Anor Londo from Dark Souls? Can a reader fall asleep with an open copy of Tom Sawyer, in order to astral project himself to a spiritual reflection of literary Mississippi, and watch personally as the narrative plays out? Could a surrealist climb into one of the paintings of Salvador Dali, walk into the common desert background that shows up in many of the latter's paintings, and find all of the set pieces Dali ever created if the Mage just looked hard enough?<br /> <br /> And if an Artist Mage paints a picture, does that automatically create an Umbral realm? It probably wouldn't be a true Horizon realm (not unless the Mage was powerful enough to create one), but would it behave otherwise like Umbral realms ought? Or does a work need to be exposed to many different people, so its presence within the collective unconscious becomes strong enough to hold a concrete spiritual shape? How far beyond a landscape's &quot;frame&quot; does that landscape extend? Is a literary realm take visual form when you visit it, or does one's perceptions extend only to text, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/IOOW6xS88VE?t=10m1s\" target=\"_blank\">Nier-style</a>? And does a realm created from a novel endlessly replay the events of that novel, or is it a living world, with living (Umbral) denizens, with their own living wills?<br /> <br /> Discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:12:04-08:00","id":1035826,"title":"","content":"That's a very good idea, and I would say that yes a &quot;powerful&quot; work of Art made by a mage (or anyone, really) will be reflected in the Astral Umbra. Maybe even to the point of creating a Spirit representing it (the Mona Lisa for Incarna?) or even a Realm.<br /> <br /> However, I don't think it will have a persistent Realm or a powerful Spirit unless it's the receptacle of powerful emotions or toughts by a lot of people. A weaker work of art might appear as it is in the Vulgata, however, to be admired by spirits and traveling mages.<br /> <br /> Related to this matter, while I haven't heard of Realms based on singular works of art in the bibliography, there are mini realms formed by dreams. Every dream it's a realm in the Dream Zone, but they vanish when you wake up. Or rather most do, some are strong enough to live longer. Since Art and dreams are strongly related, I can see they having a similar effect on some Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T15:37:08-08:00","id":1035866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035809-art-and-the-umbra?p=1035826#post1035826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related to this matter, while I haven't heard of Realms based on singular works of art in the bibliography, there are mini realms formed by dreams. Every dream it's a realm in the Dream Zone, but they vanish when you wake up. Or rather most do, some are strong enough to live longer. Since Art and dreams are strongly related, I can see they having a similar effect on some Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between a Dream and a piece of Art, of course, being that Dreams tend to be forgotten upon waking. When the Red King wakes, Looking Glass World ceases to be...unless it's the literary version, born from Lewis Carrol's writing. Dreams - and thus dream realms - tend to disappear because they are insubstantial pageant plays. But a work of Art (usually) persists, both as its physical manifestation and in the thoughts of those who view it and re-view it. Paintings displayed and their images copied for magazines, novels printed en masse, video games distributed digitally and preserved through countless let's plays. A work of Art - a product of their creator's efforts and its audience's contemplation - has staying power.<br /> <br /> By that method, an Umbral realm reflecting a work of Art - especially a famous or popular one - has as much staying power within the spirit worlds as the high umbrood courts of Egypt, Greece, Japan, and Babylon. Fitting, as these pantheons are oft preserved in the imaginations of historians and laymen alike...because of the art inspired by them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:29:47-08:00","id":1035887,"title":"","content":"A mage who has a museum of paintings in her sanctum could step sideways to the Astral Umbra and see a gallery of what would be at the same time reflections of these works, the Ideas and Feelings behind them, and a galery of portals to realms that represent them. These would conect, in turn, with the larger Realms of the genre, the artisitic movement, like the realm of Dadaism, the realm of Surrealism, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}